            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "tools/config-clang-tidy",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "A helpful tool for simplifying clang-tidy setup across projects.\n \nFew nice-to-have future improvements that could enhance the robustness and user experience of the tool:\n\nValidation of Check Names\nThe tool accepts invalid or misspelled check names without any validation. Incorporating a validation step (possibly against a known list of clang-tidy checks based on openBMC supported version ?) would prevent misconfigurations and improve reliability.\nIs there any restriction on adding new checks that aren't part of the OpenBMC-approved checklist, or is this left to the maintainer's discretion?\n\nMissing --repo Option\nIf the --repo argument is omitted, the tool still proceeds without throwing an error. providing error message would help here.\n\nDuplicate Check Handling\nCurrently, if the same check is added multiple times using the enable command. Functionally option is working as expected . no duplicate entry creates."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/config-clang-tidy",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for taking a look.\n\n> Missing --repo Option\n\nThe default becomes `.`.  This is intentional.\n\n> Duplicate Check Handling\n\nDone.\n\n> Validation of Check Names\n\nWe can have further discussion on how to handle this.  I don't have a great answer right now other than maybe eventually doing a comparison against the one in docs as part of CI and flagging repositories with extra checks.  Right now there are so many extra checks that we can't do this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/config-clang-tidy",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> Duplicate Check Handling\n\nSorry, was there something you wanted done there?  I thought you were saying that if a check was already enabled and you called `enable <check>` it would have two entries, but that doesn't seem to be the case."
                },
                {
                    "file": "tools/config-clang-tidy",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Functionally working as expected. Just for your reference, I added a note\u2014there are no warning messages. No update required."
                }
            ],
